Beam deflection and strain-energy methods (@mech-deflection-energy: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mechanical-engineering, #source "../sources/Mechanics-of-Materials-Roylance.lingua#r_7K2RYA9504FGFGJTVWHMWXD5WY", #source "../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W", #mechanical-engineering "Indeterminate-structures-support-motion-and-model-choice.lingua#r_0P7V5TZAAAS197VS41XZWWANBG") { r_4N5H6WAFTMCK0SF1TZH0SVF095
**Read:** [Modules in Mechanics of Materials — David Roylance](../sources/Mechanics-of-Materials-Roylance.lingua#r_7K2RYA9504FGFGJTVWHMWXD5WY), Beam Displacements; [Applied Mechanics of Solids — Allan F. Bower](../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W), section 5.6 and chapter 10. Work the complete displacement module and its boundary-condition problems.

Curvature connects bending moment to deflection. With a consistent sign convention and small slopes, curvature is the second derivative of transverse displacement; integrate M/(EI) and enforce the actual slope/displacement conditions. A simple support fixes transverse position but permits rotation; a clamp constrains both in the ideal beam model.

A uniform cantilever under a tip force P has tip-deflection magnitude PL³/(3EI). With P = 100 N, L = 0.5 m, E = 200 GPa and the earlier 20×40 mm section, this is 0.1953125 mm. The result depends strongly on length and the bending axis. Support flexibility may add comparable displacement.

For linear elasticity, bending strain energy is ∫ M²/(2EI) dx. Differentiating appropriate strain energy with respect to a load gives its conjugate displacement under the hypotheses of Castigliano's theorem. Include axial, shear and torsional energy when they matter. A fictitious unit load can expose a displacement at a point with no actual applied force.

**Work:** Derive the cantilever tip displacement by direct integration and energy. Extend to a stepped stiffness and combined loads. Compare predicted strain, displacement and reactions with a suitably bounded observation, including support compliance and dimensional uncertainty. Refine the beam theory when shear deformation or large rotations become significant.

**Return:** [Mechanical engineering and machine design](../Mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design.lingua#r_0017YZ63HZBZ4P4WD8DECVWE4R).
